.TH BEAM 1 "2026" "Beam" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beam \- direct file sharing between devices over a private network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beam
[\fI\-\-port PORT\fR] [\fI\-\-no\-browser\fR] [\fI\-\-idle\-timeout DUR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Beam shares files between phones and computers on the same Wi-Fi network,
with no internet and no accounts. Beam keeps no side files: settings apply
to the running session (the owner's browser keeps a copy in localStorage),
the access log lives in memory, and shared files live in
\fI~/Downloads/Beam\fR.
If the server is down it is started and the page opens in the browser.
The join link/QR inside the page is shared with guest devices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port PORT\fR
Server port (fixed default 2004: http://<ip>:2004).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR
Do not open the browser.
.TP
\fB\-\-idle\-timeout DUR\fR
Auto shutdown after this long without activity (default 5h, 0 disables).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/libexec/beam/Beam\fR
Static server binary (run via \fBbeam\fR).
.TP
\fI~/Downloads/Beam/\fR
The one well-known share folder.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Project README (docs/ folder of the source tree).
